once upon a time  HTC was a thriving phone maker with lots  of popular phones released last year the  HTC One garnered awards and rave reviews  but then things took a turn for the  worse nobody bought it the villains were  likely HTC's own supply issues and an  aggressive marketing campaigns from  Samsung and Apple now if this were a  real fairy tale the new HTC One m8 would  become the king of the Android kingdom  after all the m8 has a brand new design  and even more powerful camera and it's  gonna be available at all US carriers  this week for 199 dollars but if people  turn their back on the first best  Android phone ever will they embrace a  new one wrapped in a solid piece of  smooth metal with rounded edges this is  one nice phone to hold though I wish the  company had stuck with the 4.7 inch  screen the bigger 5-inch 1080p screen is  beautiful it's just harder to navigate  with one hand  HTC did remove the physical buttons on  the phone and integrated them right on  the screen to save space but still it's  longer than most phones and that's  because of the boom sound speakers yeah  the name is unfortunate but the speakers  actually do produce a pretty loud sound  there are also some really cool camera  upgrades you'll notice here on the back  that there are two cameras this is the  main camera but this one up here  actually collects focus information or  depth information so you can tap on a  photo and then refocus it it works  surprisingly well and then there are  loads of other fun photo tricks too  I didn't say they were useful the photos  themselves captured by the ultra pixel  camera are decent though not as crisp as  the ones I've taken with the iPhone 5s  that said the simple camera interface is  better than any I've seen on a phone an  Ellen DeGeneres is going to love this  there's a selfie mode which snaps photos  to the improve front-facing camera and  there's a tool to make your face look  thinner not that any of us need that HTC  has made some improvements to its blink  widget which brings in news and social  media feeds but I didn't use it much I  did use the double tap to wake feature a  lot though and if you buy this awesome  $50 case you can see the time and the  weather right through it it totally  looks like a light break not everything  is perfect though when you make  selections on the screen it makes these  electric shock sounds I could not  disable that fast enough the battery  life also could be better and the  keyboard is hard to type on in the end  the HTC One m8 may not break a lot of  new ground but it's still one of the  greatest Android phones ever made no it  isn't water-resistant and it doesn't  have a heart rate monitor like Samsung's  Galaxy s5 but the software and the  hardware design are better unless your  Samsung or Apple the smartphone business  these days is in a fairytale in a  perfect story more people would ignore  the ads listen to me and live happily  ever after  with this phone
 

